From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 9 Jul 2026 18:10:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ports/arkweb: add on-device regression tests (scroll, nav,
 render, multi-webview, vsync)

Extend the smoke-test harness with feature tests, sharing helpers/fixtures
via a new conftest.py (device connection, uinput/hilog/screenshot helpers,
JPEG-tolerant pixel classifiers). Each test relaunches the app on a
self-describing data: page and asserts via hilog markers + screenshot pixel
checks:

- render: solid colour bands paint correctly (WebRender/surfman pipeline)
- scroll: touch-drag moves content (guards the batched-OnTouchMove fix)
- navigation: link tap navigates, history back returns
- multi-webview: SplitPage's two concurrent surfaces both render
- vsync: a CSS animation advances, and hilog shows the OHOS Vsync framework
  servicing our named "ServoArkWeb-<id>" connection -- proving frames are
  vsync-driven with no engine instrumentation

Refactor test_ime.py onto the shared conftest. Exempt the pytest files from
ruff ANN (type-annotation) rules, matching Servo's existing per-file ignores
for test code.

Validated on rk3568: 12 tests green (uv run per file, or
`python -m pytest ports/arkweb/tools`).

Validation: Test by running uv run --with pytest --with hdc-py --with pillow python -m pytest ports/arkweb/tools on a device.
AI-assisted: Yes (agent session; implementation and on-device testing)

Clear hilog before the vsync assertion rather than relying on the launch-time clear.

The premise the check was written on -- that the OHOS Vsync framework logs the
serviced connection once -- is wrong: it re-logs periodically, roughly every 10s
while the connection is serviced. What actually breaks the check is the 256K
hilog buffer, which holds only ~4400 lines on a busy device and wraps within
seconds, so a line emitted during launch is evicted long before the assertion
reads it. The test therefore failed whenever it ran last in the full suite (after
~5 minutes of log traffic) and passed standalone against a quiet buffer.

Clear the buffer at the start of the check so the next servicing lands in an empty
one, and widen the window to 40s to cover the measured re-log interval.

Validation: Test by running the full suite (uv run --with pytest --with hdc-py --with pillow python -m pytest ports/arkweb/tools) so test_frames_are_vsync_driven runs last, after the buffer has been churned by every preceding test.
AI-assisted: Yes (agent session; implementation and on-device testing)
Signed-off-by: Jonathan Schwender <jschwender@posteo.net>
